  "notes": "One game from the initialized NVRAM. The trough release switch 44 starts closed. Two coins on public 1 and Start (3); the host opens 44 as the ball leaves the trough and passes it through the shooter lane switch 43, pulses each CPU-fired switch for 40 ms until its coil is published (up to eight pulses; PinMAME's four-frame System 3 solenoid smoothing can hide a single short coil pulse), holds the top kicker 53 for up to 8 s until its kicker fires, drops both four-target banks, pulses every spot target, rollover and ramp switch, holds the bottom upkicker 52 for up to 8 s until its kicker fires, presses both flipper buttons, idles for 20 s and drains the ball to the outhole 54 and back to 44.",
